course: dictionary
lesson: 3985
title: Which Galicia?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can point to more than one place, so you must use the context to find the right meaning. Galician can mean a person or thing from Galicia, or the language spoken there. Look at the words around it to see which one fits.
explain: «Galician coast» and «speak Galician» show the Spanish region. Galicia is in the north-west of Spain, by the sea, and Galician is a language spoken there. Here Galician describes a place, or names a language.
explain: The sentence «The blue-and-yellow flag comes from Galician coats of arms» is about history, not Spain. The coats of arms and the year 1848 point to the old region of Galicia in Ukraine and Poland. Ask yourself: which Galicia fits these clues?
fact: Galician means from Galicia, or about its people.
fact: Galicia is a region in the north-west of Spain, and Galician is also the language spoken there, close to Portuguese.
fact: Galicia was also an old region in western Ukraine and south-east Poland, around Lviv and Kraków, which was part of Austria-Hungary until 1918.
fact: Phrases like «Galician bagpipes» and «Galician coast» usually mean the Spanish region.
fact: Galician is written with a capital G, like other names of people, places and languages.
exercise: «They went to the Galician coast for their holidays.» Where did they go? | Lviv in Ukraine | *The north-west of Spain, by the sea | Kraków in Poland
exercise: Ana says, «She can speak Galician.» What is Galician here? | A flag | *A language | A person from Lviv
exercise: «The blue-and-yellow flag comes from Galician coats of arms.» Which Galicia is meant? | The flag of Portugal | The Spanish one by the sea | A town in Austria | *The old region around Lviv and Kraków
test: «The Galician bagpipes played at the festival.» What does Galician describe? | Coats of arms from Lviv | A flag from 1918 | A language spoken in Kraków | *Bagpipes from Galicia in Spain
test: Which Galicia is meant in the words «used by Ukrainians in 1848»? | The language close to Portuguese | *The historic region in western Ukraine and south-east Poland | The bagpipes of the festival | The north-west coast of Spain
exam: Mia reads, «The Galician town was part of Austria-Hungary until 1918.» Which Galicia is meant? | *The old region around Lviv and Kraków | The language spoken near Portugal | Galician bagpipes | The north-west of Spain
